Thought: The series is trend‑dominated with very high predictability and moderate ranking stability, so a selective weighted combination based on inverse error is a reasonable first test.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: The series is strongly trend‑dominated and the diagnostics suggest a selective combination; a trimmed mean may discard extreme forecasts while retaining the core signal.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2,"rationale":"Testing trimmed mean as selective combination for trend‑dominated series"}

Thought: Given the strong trend and moderate ranking stability, I want to test a robust selective combination: median over the full pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: I’ll test a weighted strategy with softmax‐based weights on the full pool, as a distinct weighting approach that may improve over the median while keeping all models involved.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: The series is trend‑dominated with moderate ranking stability; a selective combination has worked best so far. Let’s try a different kind of combination – the DBA (dynamic Bayesian aggregation) over the full pool to see if it can exploit the model diversity.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: test a meta‑model weighted combination over the full pool (weighted w1) to see if a learned weighting improves over the current best median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a simple mean of the selective pool1 models to see if averaging a smaller, high‑correlation‑group set improves on the median full baseline, leveraging the strong trend and moderate ranking stability.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: The series is trend‑dominated with a selective‑combination hint, so a weighted blend on the small, high‑quality pool1 may beat the simple mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: The series is trend‑dominated with selective combination suggested; try a weighted mix on pool1 using inverse‑error weights to see if we can beat the current best 0.159.  

Action: evaluate_strategy  

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a full‑pool weighted combination with inverse_error weights to see if adding more models improves the selective weighted pool1 result.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: The series is trend‑dominated with high predictability; a selective combination is advised. Weighted pool1 with softmax_neg_error could sharpen the weighting compared to inverse_error and may improve on the current best score (0.159).

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: Test a selective median combination on the narrow pool1 to see if a robust, simple selective method can improve over the weighted softmax result.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: The series has a very strong trend and the leader uses a selective weighted pool1; trying a different weight method on the same pool may improve the score. I will test weighted pool1 with error_trend weights.  

Action: evaluate_strategy  

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"error_trend"}

Thought: The series is trend‑dominated with moderate ranking stability, so a selective combination that covers more diverse error groups may help. I will test a weighted softmax‑negative‑error combination on the broader pool3, which includes rf, CWT_rf, DWT_rf, FT_rf, DWT_catboost and ONLY_CWT_rf to increase diversity.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool3","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

